<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beornwulf of Mercia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 826</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beornwulf was king of Mercia from 823 to 826, after displacing Ceolwulf I. In 825 he was decisively defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egbert-of-wessex">Ecgberht of Wessex</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ellendun">Battle of Ellendun</a>, after which Kent, Surrey, Sussex and Essex passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a>. Attempting to put down a revolt of the East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angles">Angles</a>, he was killed by them in 826.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beornwulf-of-mercia.jpg" alt="Beornwulf of Mercia" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG - Classical Numismatic Group · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beornwulf,_King_of_Mercia,_silver_penny_(group_I);_struck_823%E2%80%93825_AD_(obverse).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
